1 | db-architect | On branch feat/ac-w1d-authserver (draft PR 2815) add the durable storage for the assistant-channel authorization server. READ FIRST the storage posture note near the top of apps/api/internal/service/assistant_auth.go, which specifies exactly what is needed, and apps/api/db/CLAUDE.md for conventions. Deliver one timestamped migration plus sqlc queries for three tables: assistant_authorize_requests (pending browser flows: request_id hash, client_id, user_id nullable until login, code_challenge, redirect_uri, scope, browser_secret_hash, csrf_token_hash, expires_at, consumed_at), assistant_authorization_codes (code_hash, request reference, user_id, binding_id, code_challenge, redirect_uri, expires_at, consumed_at), and assistant_refresh_tokens (token_hash, family_id, binding_id, user_id, issued_at, expires_at, revoked_at, replaced_by nullable). Store hashes only, never plaintext. Queries needed by the service: insert and consume by hash for requests and codes, insert refresh, lookup refresh by hash, mark refresh replaced, revoke a whole family, revoke all families for a binding id, and a cleanup that deletes expired rows. Run make sqlc-generate or the equivalent from make help, and the migration filename gate, and paste real exit codes. Do not edit the service package; wave 2 wires it. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Commit and push to the same branch, keep the PR a draft. | feat/ac-w1d-authserver

2 | go-backend | On branch feat/ac-w1d-authserver (draft PR 2815) wire the assistant authorization service to the Postgres store that wave 1 added under apps/api/db. READ FIRST the storage posture note near the top of apps/api/internal/service/assistant_auth.go and the new sqlc code. Replace the in-memory maps for pending requests, codes and refresh families with a store interface backed by Postgres in production and by the existing memory implementation only in tests; hash every code, request id, browser secret and refresh token with SHA-256 before it touches the store; keep every guarantee already implemented on this branch (per-traveller binding identity, family revoke on reuse with an audit row, binding_id claim and per-binding liveness, browser-bound consent, fixed error descriptions) and make the critic RED tests still pass. Then rewrite the storage posture note to describe the durable design as built, and remove the long dash it currently contains. Wire the store in cmd/server/main.go. VERIFY: go build ./... and go test ./... with the race flag in apps/api, real exit codes captured directly and pasted into the PR body under Verification; update the PR body to say token state is durable. DO NOT touch api.yaml, scripts/, docs/ or .env.example. HOUSE STYLE: no long dash anywhere, no AI tool or vendor name, no Co-Authored-By trailer. Push to the same branch, keep the PR a draft. | feat/ac-w1d-authserver

